This page compares zanity with [lizard](https://github.com/terryyin/lizard) on the same source files.
Generated by `bench/parity/parity.py` on 2026-10-18, against zanity `1857167`.

# Rule by rule

Same line means zanity reports it on the tool's line, give or take one. A note identifies deliberate differences.

| Its rule | zanity rule | It fires | zanity fires | Same line | Note |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `cognitive_complexity` | `deep-nesting` | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | zanity has no cognitive complexity; it reports the nesting that drives the score |
| `cyclomatic_complexity` | `complex-function` | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) |  |
| `length` | `long-function` | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | Lizard warns past 1,000 lines; zanity flags 60 lines of code, as Power of Ten says |
| `max_nested_structures` | `deep-nesting` | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | [✗ no]($text.attrs('badge','fail')) | [✗ no]($text.attrs('badge','fail')) | Lizard warns at four nested structures and counts each elif as one more; zanity flags code nested deeper than four |
| `max_nesting_depth` | `deep-nesting` | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) |  |
| `parameter_count` | `long-parameter-list` | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | [✓ yes]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) | Lizard warns past 100 parameters; zanity flags more than four |
| `nloc` | `long-function` | [– n/a]($text.attrs('badge','none')) | [– n/a]($text.attrs('badge','none')) | [– n/a]($text.attrs('badge','none')) | No fixture: its default limit is a million lines of code. |

# Real code

## Recall

Of each tool's findings, how many zanity reports on the same lines with a mapped rule.

| Tool | Its rule | zanity rule | Note | Its findings | zanity too | Recall |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| lizard | `cyclomatic_complexity` | `complex-function` |  | 40 | 40 | [100%]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) |
| lizard | `cognitive_complexity` | `complex-function`, `deep-nesting` | zanity has no cognitive complexity; it reports the nesting that drives the score | 68 | 48 | [71%]($text.attrs('badge','partial')) |
| lizard | `max_nesting_depth` | `deep-nesting` |  | 54 | 15 | [28%]($text.attrs('badge','partial')) |
| lizard | `max_nested_structures` | `deep-nesting` | Lizard warns at four nested structures and counts each elif as one more; zanity flags code nested deeper than four | 808 | 26 | [3%]($text.attrs('badge','partial')) |

## Agreement

Of zanity's findings, how many the tool also reports. Low agreement is zanity finding what the tool doesn't, which can be either tool's mistake.

| Tool | zanity rule | zanity findings | Tool too | Agreement |
| --- | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| lizard | `complex-function` | 40 | 40 | 100% |
| lizard | `deep-nesting` | 24 | 24 | 100% |
| lizard | `long-function` | 55 | 0 | 0% |
| lizard | `long-parameter-list` | 67 | 0 | 0% |
